From 1fb39d4304c004b037f9f3cba5b05aaa807c0506 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 06:11:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Split ring4 opposite-rank relay traffic across both
 directions

Upstream-base: 236ddff04a5f5064084b46464800b70b34ec7d8c
Patch-base: 6056b0a181a5388a7a77e4192121d89a0a42d426

Keep neighbour payloads on direct QPs. Relay disjoint halves of every
physical stripe clockwise and counterclockwise, independently as their
first-hop flags arrive. Preserve the two-slot lifetime and fixed-rank
reduction; add completion flags for both fragments, including empty ones.
Bump the wire ABI so old and new peers cannot exchange incompatible flags.

Quality: transport-only; payload bytes and reduction arithmetic unchanged.
Tests: 26000 sanitizer-backed simulated collectives, directional byte
balance, unique pack delivery, independently stalled paths, wraparound,
stop/error paths, direct/mesh regressions, GPU launcher geometry/cache keys.
Hardware qualification remains required; no speed or thermal claim.
Upstream-status: local experiment, not submitted.
